Portions of the torch op names, shapes, and call conventions follow the
ComfyKitchen torch ops (int8_attention, adaln, rms_adaln, apply_rope,
stochastic_rounding_fp8). This project is independent and is not affiliated
with or endorsed by Comfy Org; compatibility with ComfyKitchen is not a goal —
existing DiT kernels are pluginized for TRT engines here.

Unmodified copies of the following ComfyKitchen CUDA sources are vendored
under src/kernel/ (Apache-2.0; each file carries a one-line vendoring notice
on top, otherwise byte-identical, original SPDX headers retained):

- backends/cuda/sage_attention/ (quant_qk_int8.cu, quant_v_int8.cu,
  sage_attn_launcher.cu and supporting .cuh)
  Derived in part from SageAttention, Copyright (c) 2024 by SageAttention
  team (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/thu-ml/SageAttention,
  commit d1a57a546c3d395b1ffcbeecc66d81db76f3b4b5).
- backends/cuda/ops/adaln.cu
- backends/cuda/ops/rms_rope.cu, rope_device.cuh
- backends/cuda/ops/per_tensor_quantize.cu
- backends/cuda/{dtype_dispatch.cuh, float_utils.cuh, utils.cuh}

